From d9b9d4d4a62df78cb6ed6b93594380238a2b06b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Brian S. Park" <brianspark@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:25:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mmvq: the 32-element Q4_K dot product for MoE experts on
 gfx1100 (RDNA3_0)

The MoE expert kernel (mul_mat_vec_q_moe) uses vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4,
which scales and converts each of its four 8-element chunks separately.
vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4_dense (r69) has the same 32-element layout and VDR
(4) and sums each sub-block's 16 products in one integer dp4a chain before
the single scale / convert / fma (exact), so on RDNA3_0 MoE takes it too.
RDNA4 and the other targets are unchanged.

gfx1100 (WSL2), Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M, r70 vs r70 + this, rocprofv3 of one
400-token request, per call: fused gate+up+GLU Q4_K experts 24.8 -> 22.3
us (-10 %), Q4_K down experts 19.4 -> 16.0 us (-18 %); total GPU time
4167 -> 4087 ms (-1.9 %).  0 scratch.  llama-bench tg256 x10, 2 rounds
alternating: 131.7 -> 133.6 t/s (+1.4 %).

Output: the summation order changes, so greedy text changes on this model;
dense models are unaffected (no MUL_MAT_ID).  Width probe PASS at P = 256
and 3584 on the MoE model; test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID q4_K 84/84.
llama-perplexity -ub 4 (the MoE mmvq path), 24 x 512 tokens, measured on
the same diff on r67 + #162: mean KLD 0.0044 against the parent, same top
token 97.0 %, PPL ratio 1.0013 +- 0.0021; for scale, the parent's own
-ub 512 (MMQ) against its -ub 4: KLD 0.0065, 95.9 %.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-vecdot.cuh | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-vecdot.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-vecdot.cuh
index ea5cec0a7..846d17867 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-vecdot.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-vecdot.cuh
@@ -34,7 +34,10 @@ static constexpr __device__ vec_dot_q_cuda_t get_vec_dot_q_cuda(ggml_type type,
         case GGML_TYPE_NVFP4:   return vec_dot_nvfp4_q8_1;
         case GGML_TYPE_Q2_K:    return vec_dot_q2_K_q8_1;
         case GGML_TYPE_Q3_K:    return vec_dot_q3_K_q8_1;
-#if defined(GGML_CUDA_Q4K_DENSE_VDR4)
+#if defined(RDNA3_0)
+        // MoE takes it too: same 32-element layout and VDR as vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4, one integer chain per sub-block
+        case GGML_TYPE_Q4_K:    return vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4_dense;
+#elif defined(GGML_CUDA_Q4K_DENSE_VDR4)
         case GGML_TYPE_Q4_K:    return moe ? vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4 : vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4_dense;
 #else
         case GGML_TYPE_Q4_K:    return moe ? vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4 : vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1;
